# Access-control rules for the lineage_ims_prop type. The type itself
# is declared in public/lineage_ims_prop.te so vendor sepolicy can
# reference it (ims_oemipc, etc.).
#
# Why this namespace exists at all:
#   The earlier `debug.ims.*` properties mapped to `debug_prop`, which
#   meant `adb shell setprop`, `dumpsys`, and any app with the broad
#   debug-prop permission could fire arbitrary IMS xfrm/ipsec/OEM-IPC
#   commands as root via the init.rc trigger chain — a real privilege
#   escalation surface. `lineage.ims.*` narrows that to:
#     - HamelinPortsImsService (system_app, platform-signed) is the
#       only userspace domain that can SET the values and bump the
#       trigger.
#     - init.rc reads them when its property trigger fires (init has
#       implicit read on all properties).
#     - Vendor helpers (ims_oemipc) read them via get_prop below.
#     - Nothing else can write.

# Only HamelinPortsImsService writes these.
set_prop(system_app, lineage_ims_prop)
